# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trim the build context.
#
# `npm run build` is `vite build` (root: client) plus `tsc -p
# tsconfig.server.json`, so the image only ever needs client/, server/,
# shared/, the package manifests and the config files at the root. Everything
# below is firmware, hardware design, sibling services or old archives that the
# Node build never reads, and it was all being shipped to the daemon on every
# build: the context measured 306 MB and took 181 s to transfer on a box with
# 2 GB of free disk.
#
# Safe to exclude because docker-compose.yml declares exactly one build context
# (the stratus service). The forecast, panel, demo and info-centre services are
# built from their own compose files under /opt, not from this directory, so
# ignoring their source here cannot affect them.
#
# The @assets vite alias points at ./attached_assets, NOT ./assets, and nothing
# imports it, so assets/ is not a build input either.

# Sibling services, built from their own compose files elsewhere.
forecast
info-centre
lightning-demo
LDS ADMIN
LDS ADMIN PANEL

# Firmware, hardware design and device tooling.
AS3935
AS3935handheld
Beacon
BeagleBone
Emulator
Lightning Detector
Quaggasklip
RPiZero SD Card
StratusLoggerV1*

# Local-only working directories.
localhost-preview
documents
demo_data
.venv
.github
.sixth

# Loose archives and database dumps left at the root.
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip
*.sql
*.sql.gz
*.pdf

# Stale source snapshots.
client.bak*
client_src.bak*
clientsrc*
server.bak*

# assets/ is not referenced by the client build (see note above).
assets
